BANDWIDTH ARM (EXPLORATORY, deviations D4): fraud, selectk/8 qubits, 250 per class
==========================================================================

  Gain from adding a bandwidth grid, in normAP:
    real labels     : mean gain +0.0029  median +0.0013  sd 0.0105  p 0.2413  (n=20)
    permuted labels : mean gain +0.0012  median +0.0000  sd 0.0313  p 0.6772  (n=20)

  The comparison that decides it:
    real gain / permuted gain = 2.53   (the classical grids measured 0.14 to 0.20 here, which is why they were left frozen)
    excess of real over permuted, paired by seed: +0.0018 [-0.0149, +0.0185]  p 0.8288

  inner CV chose bandwidth (real labels): {0.0625: 5, 0.125: 9, 0.25: 3, 0.5: 2, 1.0: 1}
    5/20 seeds selected a value on the grid boundary. Per section 7 this is descriptive, not a licence to widen again.

  absolute normAP in this cell: registered 0.9632 -> widened 0.9661

  READING, per D4: widening gained no more on real labels than on permuted ones. This is winner's curse, the registered result stands unqualified, and this arm becomes a control that strengthens H1. D4 outcome two.

